{
  "rationale": "The plant automata separate sensing and motion: G1 models the robot's perception of obstacles, and G2 models its motion capabilities. The specifications E1-E4 encode safe, coverage-oriented exploration: E1 binds clear sensing to forward/random_walk actions; E2-E3 bind left/right obstacles to directed turns; E4 encodes conservative recovery for front obstacles. The design ensures forward progress dominates, with brief, directed recovery and minimal backward or full-rotate use.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate perception and motion into distinct plant automata for modularity and clarity.",
    "Specification automata bind each perception outcome to exactly one safe, coverage-oriented action, enforcing conservative recovery and rapid return to exploration."
  ],
